    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0595" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v21/pg567"/>

                <head>365. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in the Republic of the Congo<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d365-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-07-01T18:28:00-04:00">July 1, 1963, 6:28
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Embtel 3198. General instructions contacts
                    with Port African nationalists contained CA-14448, June 24.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d365-f2"/></p>
                <p>Gist of instruction: you should not initiate or seek out contacts with these
                    nationalists. If they ask see Embassy officer, should be received by officers
                    other than Ambassador, preferably at Pol Officer level. Since GOP has post at Leo, Port Embassy should be
                    informed after meetings <pb facs="0596" n="568" xml:id="pg568"/> that
                    nationalists seen at their request, but no indication of substance should be
                    given.</p>
                <p>If nationalists press to see Ambassador and Ambassador believes direct contact by
                    him desirable, he should submit appropriate justification and request prior
                    authorization from Dept.</p>
                <p>If Embassy officers meet Holden Roberto
                    socially or otherwise, they may of course converse with him. Utmost discretion
                    required in such contacts. These occasions need not be reported to Port
                    Embassy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Ball</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d365-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d365-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, POL 17 US-AFR. Secret. Drafted by
                    High, cleared by Starrs, and approved by Whitehouse. Repeated to Lisbon, USUN, Paris for Cleveland, and Luanda.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d365-f2" n="1" xml:id="d365-f2-content">
                <p>Airgram CA-14448 to Algiers, Conakry, Dakar, Dar-es-Salaam, Elisabethville,
                    Leopoldville, Rabat, Salisbury, and USUN, June
                    24. (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
